  "body": "Part of #1509.\n\nThe first slice of #1509 adds only the Method choice to 2D Adaptive. Under Method = Trochoidal the planner's other numbers are fixed (`crates/motion/src/machining2d/adaptive_troch.rs`, `cut_lane`):\n\n- engagement limit: 90 degrees of contact, measured (the Trochoidal slot's default);\n- forward step: at most the optimal load x D (the measured ladder shortens it);\n- return between loops: a 0.3 mm microlift, or retract hops when the clearance plane is less than 0.3 mm above the top;\n- return feed: the cutting feed;\n- loop band: all the room along the medial line;\n- the Entry setting is not read (the lane bores its own helix; a note says so when Entry is not Helix).\n\nThe stand-alone Trochoidal slot exposes all of these (#220). Wanted: the same numbers on the 2D Adaptive page when Method = Trochoidal (shown only then), in the project file with defaults that keep today's path, and through `edit_operation` over MCP.\n\nWhy not derived from the optimal load: a front arc into a full-width band wraps more of the cutter than a straight wall at the same radial bite, so the straight-wall angle of the default load (45 degrees) is never met on a loop (86 degrees measured on the 34 x 16 pin at the default load).\n\nDone means: the fields are on the page under Trochoidal only (structural UI test), round-trip the project file with older files defaulting, are undoable `EditOperationParams` edits and MCP parameters, and a limit no step can hold is refused by name with the measured number.\n",
